abstract: >-
  A complete static reverse-engineering study of the ZaloPay 11.17.0 Android
  distribution (package vn.com.vng.zalopay, a 105.6 MB XAPK holding five split
  APKs). We inventory all 6,213 files (299.6 MB), parse 19 DEX files
  (60,671 classes, 351,248 methods, 243,013 strings), profile 28 native
  libraries, identify a two-vendor native hardening packer by toolchain
  forensics (clang 17.0.2 vs 21.0.0), map four co-resident application
  runtimes (Kotlin/Java, React Native, Alibaba Griver mini-apps, H5 shell),
  extract 335 URLs across 229 hosts, and enumerate a 10-item defensive risk
  register. No private keys or live credentials were recovered.
  The study is accompanied by a TypeScript-rendered MP4 film whose every
  on-screen figure is sourced from the machine-readable dataset.
